	<!-- NP v3.7.4 -->
	<a name="newsitem966534351,71840,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Thursday, August 17, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>116d Server Side Patch</b></u><br>Vircom released the new 116d Server side patch today, this patch is mainly to help servers cut down on crash problems.<br><br><b><u>T4C Dying?</b></u><br>I have heard and read many reports from players complaining that T4C is dying so I thought I would take a personal look around and here is what I found. First off most of the servers who are not very active are having some problems with the amount of players, however with servers that are active I found the following amounts of players online. *I don't want to promote any one Server over another so I will try to keep them nameless for now and let you all do the research if you are that interested in the number of players.*<br><br>I found two Servers that had more then 200 players online at once, in fact one of these servers had over 600 players online at once! (I hear they have topped over 900 players) and I found 5 servers in the 40 to 100 players online range.<br><br>I am sorry this info is not more specific but I want to keep from promoting any server over another, but if you do the research yourself you will find that T4C is far from dead and you will find many good servers with active GM's, Quests and Events and a ton of great players!<br><br>**Please Note that the World Online User's Script does not show all the players actually online since a few Servers are behind firewalls and their Players Online information is unavailable.**<br><br><b><u>Updates</b></u><br>The <a href="http://www.t4cportal.com/shopping.asp"> Server Shopping</a> page has been updated and the<a href="http://www.t4cportal.com/guilds.asp"> Guild Links</a> page has been updated. If you have a link or a update you would like to see added please email me at <a href="mailto:sbenson@t4cportal.com">sbenson@t4cportal.com</a></font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem965862883,81853,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Wednesday, August 9, 2000<small>Posted by Lady Wigglesnort<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>T4C RAW! Player Feed Back Survey</b></u><br><br><a href="http://www.t4cgamer.com/cytheria/t4c/Scroll/feedback/LW527Survey.html">ROADTRIP</a>! Time for you to visit and express yourself about the one thing you did all summer long.. T4C style..<br><br>Just click away your summertime heat, while those T4C survey numbers pile up..higher than they have EVER reached before! Then sometime RIGHT after Friday Sept 1st- Raw's closing polling date, we will show you more than one person should ever know about the honest truth about T4C. Give it to us T4C Raw! Come on over and grab it today! Lady Wigglesnort is begging for it..now! Come Sept 1st your on your own..<br></font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem965432862,34609,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Friday, August 4, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>Portal Help</b></u><br>I just wanted to take a quick minute to thank everyone who has offered to help T4C Portal with news updates but due to the volume of requests I will not be able to answer everyone but again a big thank you to everyone who took the time to write me. We will be contacting people over the next week to give us a hand.</font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem965341267,56731,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Thursday, August 3, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>Portal Looking for help</b></u><br>We are looking for one good person to help do news updates, if you are interested and believe you can do updates that would not help promote any one server and are well spoken, please email me at <a href="mailto:sbenson@t4cportal.com">sbenson@t4cportal.com</a>.<br><br><b><u>Patch Update</b></u><br>For those keeping track there was a Server side update for those servers who updated to 116 yesterday, the current patch is now at 116b.</font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem965164858,33303,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Tuesday, August 1, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>New 116 Patch</b></u><br>The new 116 patch was released today.<br><br>*** Version 1.16 Release (07/31/00 -- 11:00 EST) ***<br><br>FIX: Shift-click no longer allows player characters to turn invisible.<br>FIX: Skill descriptions are now available when right-clicking on them in the character sheet menu.<br>FIX: Previously, if someone cast a spell (except for healing spells) on someone else (including monsters or the caster himself) in the same screen as you, it would automatically put you into combat mode against that person. This no longer happens.<br>FIX: Corpses no longer disappear, unless you start lagging.<br>FIX: Antelopes no longer drop (erroneously) rough emeralds. Those items have been removed from the game (for now).<br>FIX: Bows used to benefit from the same STR bonus for damage as warriors; they now have their own set of bonuses (mostly based on AGI, also slightly based on STR).<br>FIX: You now get the correct system messages when you're missing either the bow or the quiver you need to properly use ranged weapons.<br>FIX: Targetting problems have been resolved.<br>FIX: The spell Minor Combat Sense now affects Archery as well as the Attack skill.<br>FIX: The following items now affect the Archery skill as well as the Attack skill: Crude orcish necklace, Ring of accuracy, Amulet of precision, Ring of confidence, Orcish wristband, & Minotaur clan ring. You must first UNEQUIP them, then re-equip them to benefit from the "new" bonus.<br>FIX: The online context-sensitive help has been updated for the spells that now also affect the Archery skill.<br>FIX: All login box information is now saved immediately upon pressing the connect button.<br>FIX: Item names that are too long (in Buy/Sell boxes) are now clipped; you can see the full name by right-clicking on the name (which will also display the item's requirements at the same time).<br>FIX: [FRENCH VERSION ONLY] Le graphique pour le carquois pour les flèches en os a été corrigé.<br>FIX: [FRENCH VERSION ONLY] Le mode graphique "haute qualité" fonctionne désormais comme il faut et peut être sélectionné par le joueur.<br>FIX: [FRENCH VERSION ONLY] Changé "Prochain niveau!" pour "Vous avez gagné un niveau!" et "clic double" pour "double clic".<br>FIX: [FRENCH VERSION ONLY] "Dodge" et "Attack" sont maintenant traduits en français.<br>FYI: Just like melee combat, ranged weapons are affected by the following skills: Armor Piercing, Powerful Blow & Stun Blow.</font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem964629483,33364,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Wednesday, July 26, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>Text Macros</b></u><br>I have had several people email me if Text Macros were removed? Yes they have been removed, you must have a GM flag to do Text Macros now (Many Servers and Vircom felt the macros were needed for GM's but players were only using them to abuse the game).<br><br><b><u>Welcome Cyberwar</b></u><br>We would like to welcome the newest Server <a href="http://www.cyberwar.com/t4c/index2.html">Cyberwar</a> to the T4C community! It's always good to see the community growing.<br><br><b><u>Archer Changes?</b></u><br>Tabaxus of Gamerealm had emailed Vircom asking about the damage for archery and got the following response.<br><br>"Archery, STR bonus vs AGI bonus: We will modify the damage bonus for ranged weapons to be based mostly on AGI and slightly on STR rather than on STR alone."</font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem964548559,83589,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Tuesday, July 25, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>Bow Info</b></u><br>Here's a list of all of the bows and arrows along with their reqs and costs for +1 and +2. Archery trainers that I've found so far are Kalastor, the Lurker and Doremas, but there may be more. Quivers contain unlimited arrows, and have no reqs. Ashwood bows and Wooden arrows can be bought in LH, Elm bows and Pinpoint arrows can be bought in WH and Hickory bows and Bone-tipped arrows can be bought in SS. Ashwood and Elm +1 and +2 bows are purchased from the Arakas +1 and +2 dealers, while Hickory +1 and +2 bows are purchased from the Raven's Dust +1 and +2 dealers. I've found that the higher the str req, the slower the fire rate of the bow.<br><br>Bow			Reqs		Cost	+1 Cost	+2 Cost<br>Ashwood flatbow	None		29	87	290<br>Ashwood longbow	13 str, 24 agi	605	1815	6050<br>Ashwood reflex bow	17 str, 39 agi	2361	7083	23610<br>Elm flatbow		15 str, 53 agi	5266	15798	52660<br>Elm longbow		18 str, 68 agi	9323	27969	93230<br>Elm reflex bow		22 str, 82 agi	14529	43587	145290<br>Elm recurve bow		29 str, 97 agi	20887	62661	208870<br>Hickory flatbow		22 str, 126 agi	37053	111159	370530<br>Hickory longbow		27 str, 140 agi	46861	140583	468610<br>Hickory reflex bow	31 str, 155 agi	57821	173463	578210<br>Hickory recurve bow	40 str, 169 agi	69930	209790	699300<br>Hickory compound bow	49 str, 184 agi	83191	249573	831910<br><br>Quiver				Cost<br>Wooden arrows (unlimited)	100<br>Pinpoint arrows (unlimited)	1500<br>Bone-tipped arrows (unlimited)	15000<br><br>All of these can be bought inn Arakas or Raven's dust. Perhaps there are quests or monster drops with unique bows or quivers. the (unlimited) next to the quiver name suggests that there are quivers that DON'T have unlimited arrows, we'll just wait and see. This list is a work in progress, please e-mail any corrections or additions to prophet_t4c@yahoo.com<br><br>-Prophet<br><br><br><b><u>New 115a Server Side Fix</b></u><br>A new 115a Server side fix patch was released, it is recommended servers running 115 apply this fix right away.</font></td></tr></table><p>
<a name="newsitem964197244,17355,"></a>
<table border="0" width="93%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tr><td width="100%" bgcolor="#6600CC"><font face="Arial" size="2" color="#000000"><b><font color="#ffffff">Friday, July 21, 2000<small>Posted by Shane<br></small></b></font></td></tr><tr><td width="100%"><font face="Arial" size="2"><BR><b><u>115 Release Notes</b></u><br>*** Version 1.15 Release (07/20/00 -- 14:00 EST) ***<br><br>FIX: Corrected graphical bugs.<br>FIX: Corrected numerous typos on NPCs.<br>FIX: Corrected some blocking issues.<br>FIX: Resolved "invalid pointer" problem.<br>FIX: NPC Gwen no longer babbles (she was repeating herself).<br>FIX: Spells in auto-combat stop working if the target goes invisible or hides successfully.<br>FIX: Resolved one occurrence of the Dead Player Standing problem.<br>FIX: There is now a system message explaining that you can't drop an item (when the item is no-drop in the database).<br>FIX: Prevented the cheat that allowed permanent spell effects.<br>FIX: It's no longer necessary to activate combat mode (ctrl-c) to fight Jarko.<br>FIX: Brother Harforr said he would charge you X GPs for heals, but failed to take the gold (he takes it, now).<br>FIX: The safe in Silversky can no longer be attacked.<br>FIX: These items can now be sold to any vendor in the game (they couldn't before): Jade Ring of Sorcery, Ethereal Amulet, Tower Shield and Nature's Garb.<br>FIX: Re-casting a spell or reusing an item from the effect icon (top left of the screen) now works perfectly.<br>FIX: Integrated club weapon appearance into the game.<br>FIX: Jarko's Spellbook (item) is now non-droppable.<br>FIX: NPC Gwel used to sell all ringmail items except ringmail girdle.<br>FIX: The game no longer says "Level Up" when you enter the game.<br>FIX: Liurn Clar now charges 100 GP * your level to teleport you to Raven's Dust instead of the old flat fee of 10,000 GPs.<br>FIX: Some monster (demon, atrocity) names were displayed too low and overlapped on the monster's graphics.<br>FIX: You can now click on an item effect (i.e. torch) to re-use that item (if there's still one in your backpack). You also get a message telling you how many you have left in your inventory.<br>FIX: Properly implemented AGI requirements within the game (you'll get error messages if you don't have enough AGI to equip/use an item).<br>FIX: Spell "Plague" now has a description (right-click).<br>FIX: Removed halo around shop signs.<br>FIX: Turn Undead now more powerful if the character has spent over 2 pts of WIS per level (on average).<br>FIX: If a file is missing, an improved error message asks you to run the Safe Mode.<br>FIX: Untrapped a Taunting Horror that spawned in a mountain.<br>FIX: A bug prevented WebDownload.DLL from properly copying SETUP.EXE in Win98.<br>FIX: Rondy no longer becomes invisible after attacking you.<br>FIX: Improved the link to the players' manual on the website (there was a problem when upgrading/switching versions).<br>FIX: There is no more silence between two different music zones.<br>FIX: It's no longer possible to cast the Poison spell from within a no-PvP area.<br>FIX: The Poison spell (water element) wasn't doing as much damage as it should have against certain water-vulnerable creatures.<br>FIX: Acknowledgement message now confirms you've really learned the spell you were trying to learn.<br>FIX: The rules for experience loss due to character death have been modified. The penalty is now applied ONLY to the XP acquired since you last went up a level.<br>FIX: Modified opening hours of some NPCs. Now open 24 hours a day: Boreas, Mithrand & Greyar Eedy. Now only asleep a 1/3 of the time (instead of half the time): Celydia, Rhodar, Taliron and Kiadus.<br>FIX: Modified the red cape to use the new cape graphic.<br>FIX: Monsignor Damien now responds properly to you when swearing allegiance to Ogrimar.<br>FIX: It is no longer possible to put gold as a macro.<br>FIX: The inn sign has been adjusted so that it's still "readable" when flipped.<br>NEW: RANGED WEAPONS!!!<br>NEW: In-game speech now has a black outline to make it more legible over pale backgrounds.<br>NEW: The chat interface channel now displays the number of users in any channel (and the Main Channel displays the number of users currently online).<br><br><b><u>New 115 Patch Released</b></u><br>The new 115 patch was released today, the new patch includes the long awaited Archer and also includes quite a few bug fixes, I will post the release notes once we get them.</font></td></tr></table><p>

